   <media:description>University of Florida researchers at the @FloridaMuseum are using tiny, solar-powered radio transmitters to track monarch butterflies as they travel through North Central Florida. Light enough to ride on a monarch’s back, the tags will help scientists better understand where the butterflies go, how they navigate and how to support their conservation.

